  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 228 AM EDT Sat May 9 2026\n\n- Thunderstorms SE Lower Michigan this Afternoon\n\nA cold front pushes through today with modest moisture and \ninstability across the southeast forecast area to initiate a line\nof storms in the afternoon. High resolution CAMS show most of the\nheavier storms will moves south and east of Ingham to Jackson\nCounties, but it will be a close call. The threat should end as\nthe cold front clears the area by 5 pm.\n\n- Frost/Freeze the Next Three Nights\n\nCool high pressure builds in for tonight with clearing skies and\ndiminishing winds. This will allow good radiational cooling\nconditions and another night of frost and freezing temperatures\nfor the northern forecast area. A Freeze Warning and Frost\nAdvisory has been issued for that area. Sunday and Monday nights \nwill be even colder with an expected expansion of the Frost/Freeze\nheadlines for most or all of the forecast area. Low pressure\nwill bring rain on Tuesday as a clipper type low moves through in\nfast northwest flow regime.",
